WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.510
In 2024, in sub-Saharan Africa, 47.1 babies
in every 1,000 born alive died before

2
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.250
their first birthday.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.430
The world average was 27.7.

4
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.650
In the UK, it was 4.1.

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.190
This is the infant mortality rate:
a key measure of development.

6
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.130
The WHO says the leading causes of death
in young children are largely preventable

7
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.610
or treatable.

8
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.590
So why do so many babies still die?

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.550
Do these diseases simply have no cure?

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.730
In this mission, you'll see where
infant mortality is highest,

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.570
and find out what babies die of.

12
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.670
Then you'll track how the
rate has changed since 1990,

13
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.530
and what the figures can hide.

14
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:50.970
Your mission: explain why so many babies
in sub-Saharan Africa die from preventable

15
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.800
causes.
